difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "393bef1a-778c-53b8-a73e-75ffc95e3405" :question/math-academy-id "q-181958" :question/problem "Which of the following is a schematic of the Cartesian product $A\\times B$ for $A={p,q}$ and $B={w,z}?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $B$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/6baae52e45d00d31eac732a23be655b648765c27cfcdc667c511b176d5bbbc88.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B.$\n\nOur completed $A\\times B$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/38e9d12b0c09ae066149d95235a6918712214edc147c57775da2d880b584cb9e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Schematic for a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "710c12de-5d01-5b08-bbc9-ef2f623d067e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307287} {:answer/id #uuid "788ab1c9-a77b-5ebe-9ea8-c085ff8a685f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307288} {:answer/id #uuid "b8255dae-9506-5229-829b-b36f76b3e4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307289} {:answer/id #uuid "6519ab84-a21e-5fcd-a8e6-ab23a33f8df0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307290} {:answer/id #uuid "97963324-1fd9-5c84-9ade-883794dce552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "710c12de-5d01-5b08-bbc9-ef2f623d067e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307287} :answer-field/id #uuid "f33d4708-7849-502c-b078-0d0aa6a56353" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5132636e-fc5c-596d-8624-67ad2af0f5ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-181963" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/cb3e6ef6a832f2adbbc5e096bddf2c4f6a0445fbd77a71df5617298f8dad2e51.png)\n\nBy finding the missing entries in the schematic shown above for $A\\times B,$ where $A={a,b,c}$ and $B={2,4,6},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(4,b)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times B,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/57d053cca53046f02201540e655030a37ba8f7a2811e7dc724cf30ca9fd3c072.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(4,b)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Schematic for a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f50383ed-f5db-52e3-9a47-a3279815a4eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376510} {:answer/id #uuid "f8940f2e-49fb-5589-9dc6-c528426afa92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376511} {:answer/id #uuid "d126857b-cc94-59e3-b2ee-2b1f147403ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376512} {:answer/id #uuid "43838c97-b0ad-59b9-835c-28b6c838d88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376513} {:answer/id #uuid "a41d1e81-acce-543a-84fe-97d6f5ebd73b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43838c97-b0ad-59b9-835c-28b6c838d88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376513} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6eef2c1-ec7a-5ddc-8ccf-069d417389ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e64fee60-df13-5cd7-874f-46a2aaf62710" :question/math-academy-id "q-181975" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/bf1c37a92b184cb3e6c81bbd2d653008f5eff0e3b2131f2f297a336881661c22.png)\n\nUsing the visual schematic above for the Cartesian product ${A}^{2}$ for $A={p,q,r},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(q,q)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(p,r)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- ${q}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The set ${A}^{2}$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product $A\\times A.$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times A,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set $(A)$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set $(A)$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/919ad6e16dcd1d8f02e8c15c7bd1dfa15f67232c99706dfbc1239e1f9a0f99e5.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(q,q)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- $(p,r)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- ${q}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Schematic for a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "722f8484-c1fd-5fc6-9211-43dd574c1ed2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376517} {:answer/id #uuid "478e75fb-b80e-53b7-8e4e-447dba895fe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376518} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca6e134-084c-54cb-89b5-c9ee8058fb29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376519} {:answer/id #uuid "a23b5cde-f7f6-5d10-9e29-96160adf9dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376520} {:answer/id #uuid "1b487fd2-1d85-551b-97fc-2febb4244949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "722f8484-c1fd-5fc6-9211-43dd574c1ed2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376517} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e4a7b22-0dec-5f23-80d6-3844ff0f3066" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79fb0aa2-93da-5faf-b8b1-c14f9fd9a036" :question/math-academy-id "q-181978" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/d6ee87bd861491394c6643679f62cb4b94436bf2777bd2436b3169e779736e2c.png)\n\nUsing the visual schematic above for the Cartesian product ${A}^{2}$ for $A={h,k},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- ${h}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(h,k)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(k,k)\\in {A}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The set ${A}^{2}$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product $A\\times A.$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times A,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set $(A)$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set $(A)$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/507f8f6306c309d5e894cfb1dabfc2019f371911f7878b196e1f329f1b37dfa6.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- ${h}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}\\,\\times $\n\n- $(h,k)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- $(k,k)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aaacb1e-c2da-53bc-8878-dd22627e510c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376524} {:answer/id #uuid "563e81b1-655f-5a05-b10f-268ecf7edc0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376525} {:answer/id #uuid "3b5e2e68-984a-53a8-9d14-32c968111bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376526} {:answer/id #uuid "82c79237-d222-5d60-827f-f0cd705109ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376527} {:answer/id #uuid "dae33b17-2263-5ab0-be7b-aa431c7a0743" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b5e2e68-984a-53a8-9d14-32c968111bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376526} :answer-field/id #uuid "aae0eef6-40bd-5f34-b756-3ff8abbd6b9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb50129d-e949-518d-bacb-a24c9bd785b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-182009" :question/problem "For the sets $A={k,m},$ $B={-1,3,5},$ and $C=A\\times B,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(-1,k)\\in C$\n- $(k,m)\\in C$\n- $(m,3)\\in C$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A\\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/c660ff6d042bdf228387e5ad55651f02b136f738a2e4fa99c3ef3b3faef3e3c5.png)\n\nHence, the set $C=A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nC={(k,-1),(k,3),(k,5),(m,-1),(m,3),(m,5)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "134b9ac0-8f8f-5c45-842e-f32eda158ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376531} {:answer/id #uuid "07821f28-42c9-54e4-83e8-12329924de3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376532} {:answer/id #uuid "8bdab1ed-b5d5-50ea-b858-c3dec60ca751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376533} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ac0495-5c45-5f29-9a3b-3db2335630cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376534} {:answer/id #uuid "a487de39-b238-5ac4-a5d8-345740c51dcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a487de39-b238-5ac4-a5d8-345740c51dcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376535} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9c769e3-9521-5110-a627-7d69f08abd63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c22f43e7-cf77-5abc-b7e7-1898f3ecf81a" :question/math-academy-id "q-182011" :question/problem "For the sets $X={x,z},$ $Y={a,b},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(a,x)\\in Z$\n- $(z,a)\\in Z$\n- $(z,z)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/b73e7aeb017bd9f7c50f7d110c7933763834eb391ac4a3e97d25f4e587a8a3d4.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(x,a),(x,b),(z,a),(z,b)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376536 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12ef23d3-7ce9-5c60-a2d7-8870ea55bb5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376538} {:answer/id #uuid "166b602d-1ec2-5b5c-8f1b-e160695207f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376539} {:answer/id #uuid "34e84b6d-44af-5ac3-85b7-fd72b7d7ee17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376540} {:answer/id #uuid "f03514de-d215-5c39-ac83-2c490c9d4a6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376541} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee8b030-45e0-5f4e-bcfc-699eeb8ef6e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "166b602d-1ec2-5b5c-8f1b-e160695207f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376539} :answer-field/id #uuid "075dadd1-c068-5900-811f-367049667ea3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7feb18aa-af78-566b-b397-4449c64ec229" :question/math-academy-id "q-182020" :question/problem "For the sets $Z={t,u}$ and $Y=Z\\times Z,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(u,t)\\in Y$\n- $(u,t,u)\\in Y$\n- $({t}^{2},{u}^{2})\\in Y$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $Z\\times Z$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $Z$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Z.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${Z}^{2}=Z\\times Z$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/fa14e54c0518f8f5e64d3ccb4f725bd0b3804fb197d7b90320398ebbf09d68d4.png)\n\nHence, the set $Y=Z\\times Z$ is given by\n\n$$\nY={(t,t),(t,u)(u,t),(u,u)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a64cb45a-380c-594a-b48f-cf427dfc3bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376545} {:answer/id #uuid "06801011-2bb7-51f4-ab64-a6f7a9955e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376546} {:answer/id #uuid "65105d81-37f0-59c8-85f2-879bfc214dcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376547} {:answer/id #uuid "f213756c-e40e-5f0c-854b-0434d4ec1e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376548} {:answer/id #uuid "63c0ce15-e25b-594a-8f39-4be2b77ba006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06801011-2bb7-51f4-ab64-a6f7a9955e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376546} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd5cca6-718d-578f-b0ba-5709bbcd077c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fef8c320-85d2-5334-8cb1-417e3b026ac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-182022" :question/problem "For the sets $Z={-3,6,-9}$ and $Y=Z\\times Z,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(-3,6,-3)\\in Y$\n- $(-3,-9)\\in Y$\n- $(-9,6)\\in Y$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $Z\\times Z$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $Z$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Z.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${Z}^{2}=Z\\times Z$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/0c58bf1f025cc4960ce3b9dc8e1bc3bf474a521473833b27d136fd77fd6b814a.png)\n\nHence, the set $Y=Z\\times Z$ is given by\n\n$$\nY={(-3,-3),(-3,6),(-3,-9),(6,-3),(6,6),(6,-9),(-9,-3)(-9,6),(-9,-9)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88fb08f1-03f1-5b04-8b48-4b153e522040" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36f532d4-2b8e-5929-85a2-24e97ed3e917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376552} {:answer/id #uuid "25bc7f84-5389-59b3-8522-677e2a2440b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376553} {:answer/id #uuid "77d8c963-1b1f-5487-a6c8-246d58e67b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376554} {:answer/id #uuid "55632ff7-1de7-59b9-9fb5-68feddb79b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376555} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7bce74-02da-51bb-bda2-f6f61c546172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36f532d4-2b8e-5929-85a2-24e97ed3e917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376552} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a19d4f3-8b19-5322-a1c0-55924f93baab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4bd15135-eb4b-5dc2-8e6d-5dc565bcbdfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-80893" :question/problem "What is the cardinality of $X\\times Z$ for $X={11,12,13,...,20}$ and $Z={1,6,8,16,24,30}?$" :question/worked-solution "For any two finite sets $X$ and $Z,$ the cardinality of $X\\times Z$ is\n\n$$\n|X\\times Z|=|X|\\cdot |Z|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|X\\times Z| & =|X|\\cdot |Z| \\\\  & =10\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88fb08f1-03f1-5b04-8b48-4b153e522040" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Cardinality of a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d40d7fc-907f-5fa2-a318-268fe70d60dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376559} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c57ee1-fc50-5107-b12e-b1c30ceda120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376560} {:answer/id #uuid "73f1f8b3-ce3f-53ef-9d6b-cb50a5a3e29e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376561} {:answer/id #uuid "f811f3b8-b901-5141-9937-f14e11735386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376562} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3e2085-cff5-5985-8975-f0b740d06dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d40d7fc-907f-5fa2-a318-268fe70d60dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376559} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdfe2dd7-4f93-5123-add8-3168b3cf097c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48dac89a-a795-5667-9f70-b4b4b3a1e414" :question/math-academy-id "q-80897" :question/problem "What is the cardinality of $K\\times M$ for $K={0,3,4,11,15}$ and $M={d,e,f}?$" :question/worked-solution "For any two finite sets $K$ and $M,$ the cardinality of $K\\times M$ is\n\n$$\n|K\\times M|=|K|\\cdot |M|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|K\\times M| & =|K|\\cdot |M| \\\\  & =5\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
